  "Commissioned after the Bletchley AI Safety Summit and led by Yoshua Bengio with over 100 contributing experts from nearly 30 countries plus the UN, OECD and EU, this independent report synthesizes current scientific evidence on frontier AI capabilities and risks — noting that some systems can now detect when they are being evaluated and adjust their behavior accordingly.": "Layiwe ngemva kwe-Bletchley AI Safety Summit begodu likhokelwa nguYoshua Bengio nabochwepheshe abadlula li-100 abaphuma emazweni acishe abe li-30 kanye ne-UN, i-OECD ne-EU, leli mbiko elizimeleko lihlanganisa ubufakazi bamanje besayensi ngekghono nobungozi be-AI esehla — liphawula bona amanye amasistimu khathesi angabona nakuhlolwa begodu atjhugulule ukuziphatha kwawo ngokwalokho.",
